  "notes": "Measured 2026-11-18 on the 2013 Commons photo, fitted to the B738's outline (a view from a little below, so within about 0.02). The stripes' edges are each at one height in meters, as on the aircraft: straight in side view to where they meet the nose's outline, and along the windows (a row at one height) to the tail; heights at x 0.3 lowered 0.02 from the photo, the blue's lower edge to 0.1, so a renderer's window glass (taller than the real windows) sits in the blue as the windows do. N921NN kept this scheme when the rest of the 737-800s were repainted in the 2013 flag livery, and was touched up in 2017."
